# Ledgerline — environment.
#
# Copy to `.env` and fill in. `.env` and `.env.local` are gitignored; **this file is
# committed**, so it must never contain a real secret. It is the documentation of the
# credential surface, and `plan.md`'s deferred tasks are mostly the lines below that are
# still blank.
#
# Next.js reads env files from its own project root (`apps/web`), not the monorepo root.
# `apps/web/.env.local` is a symlink to the root `.env` so there is exactly one copy and
# the two cannot drift.
#
# WIRED   = shipping code reads it today; the app fails loudly without it.
# PENDING = the task is not built. Setting the variable does nothing yet.


# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Database — task 7.7                                                    [WIRED]
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# **This MUST name `ledgerline_app`, not Neon's default owner role.**
#
# Postgres exempts a table's owner from row-level security unless the table is FORCEd, and
# exempts a superuser even then. Neon's default connection string IS the owner. Connect as
# it and every RLS policy in migration 0002 does exactly nothing — no error, no warning,
# and every test written against that connection passes with the policies deleted. There is
# a passing test in `rls.test.ts` asserting the owner sees both tenants' rows; it reads like
# a bug and it is the documentation.
#
# Migration 0002 creates `ledgerline_app` NOLOGIN with no password ("a password in a
# migration is a password in git"). The deployment grants LOGIN and sets the secret here.
#
# Must be the WebSocket driver's URL (`neon-serverless`), never `neon-http`: the HTTP driver
# has no transactions, so `withTenant()` cannot `set_config(..., is_local => true)`, so
# `app.tenant_id` is never set, so every policy evaluates against NULL and every query
# returns nothing.
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://ledgerline_app:PASSWORD@HOST.neon.tech/ledgerline?sslmode=require


# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The crons — apps/web/vercel.json                                       [WIRED]
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Vercel sends `Authorization: Bearer $CRON_SECRET` on scheduled invocations.
#
# **A missing secret is a refusal, never a bypass.** `isCronRequest()` returns false when
# this is unset — the tempting `if (!secret) return true`, so it "works in development", is
# how the check ships disabled. A public triage endpoint is one a stranger can run against
# our model bill, or use to *drain* the poll backlog.
#
# Generate: openssl rand -hex 32
CRON_SECRET=

# The single tenant the dashboard and the crons act for, until Clerk is bound (task 7.6).
#
# Deliberately an environment variable rather than a header or `?tenant=` — a tenant id a
# client could set is not a stub for auth, it is a hole, and holes ship.
LEDGERLINE_TENANT_ID=

# Base URL of the carrier's recording API. The retention cron (Step 8.6) refuses to run
# without it: blanking transcripts while the audio survives would report `recordingsFailed: 0`
# — a green run that deleted none of the recordings. No archive, no retention pass.
RECORDING_ARCHIVE_URL=


# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The model — three call sites                                     [SEE WARNING]
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Read TODAY by `apps/web/app/api/cron/triage/route.ts`, which constructs an
# `AnthropicTriager`. `packages/extraction` (slot extraction), `packages/faq` (answer
# selection), and `packages/triage` (correction classification) all bind
# `@anthropic-ai/sdk`, and `packages/anthropic` is their shared vendor boundary.
#
# Nothing here has ever called a live model. Every test drives an injected `fetch` against
# hand-authored fixtures.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# **NOT READ BY ANY CODE YET.** The Groq migration is not implemented.
#
# Groq is not a drop-in for the Anthropic SDK in this repo, and the gap is not the key:
#
#   1. Three request builders + three response parsers. Anthropic returns `tool_use` content
#      blocks; Groq (OpenAI-compatible) returns `tool_calls`. `packages/anthropic`'s outage
#      taxonomy and wire-level test transport are Anthropic-shaped.
#   2. Every committed replay fixture is an Anthropic response body. All of them would need
#      re-authoring — and they are the reason the suite needs zero live model calls.
#   3. `thinking: {type: "disabled"}` is Anthropic-only.
#   4. **The cost model dies.** §10.5 and task 5.5 rest on Anthropic prompt caching
#      (`cache_control` breakpoints, `cache_read_input_tokens`). Groq has no equivalent
#      breakpoint API, so the "nothing in the cached prefix may vary per call" convention
#      needs re-deriving rather than porting.
#   5. Groq has no embeddings endpoint either, so task 6.6 still needs a third vendor.
#
# What makes it *bounded* is the architecture: all three call sites sit behind ports
# (`SlotExtractor`, `FaqAnswerer`, `CorrectionTriager`), so nothing above them changes.
GROQ_API_KEY=

# Which Groq models, once the migration lands. Extraction and FAQ selection are latency-
# critical (p95 first word < 1.2s); triage is a nightly batch and can afford a bigger model.
# Unverified: no Groq model has ever been scored on critical-slot accuracy here, and
# VoiceAgentBench is the reason that is not a safe assumption.
GROQ_EXTRACTION_MODEL=
GROQ_TRIAGE_MODEL=


# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The CRM — one token, one tenant                                        [WIRED]
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Set exactly one, matching `tenants.crm_provider`.
#
# `crmForTenant()` reads the token from here because there is no OAuth flow and no vault
# (task 7.5). That is correct for one tenant and a *lie* for two — so it **refuses** a
# tenant whose `crm_credentials_enc` is anything but the `env` sentinel, rather than quietly
# polling their jobs with the first tenant's token. A cross-tenant CRM write is the worst
# bug this system could have, and it must not be reachable by forgetting to finish a task.
HOUSECALL_PRO_TOKEN=
JOBBER_TOKEN=


# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Not yet wired — the ports exist, nothing constructs them             [PENDING]
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# `GoogleGeocoder` takes an `apiKey` in its options and no code path in `apps/web` builds
# one yet. Google Maps Platform → Address Validation API.
GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY=

# Telephony (tasks 4.2 / 4.6). No SIP trunk, no LiveKit room, no realtime model — nothing
# has ever answered a phone.
#
# **The one compliance rule with no test behind it lives here: the carrier's own recording
# switch must be OFF.** Twilio records from the moment a call is answered if asked, and
# those seconds precede the AI disclosure. No code in this repo can reach that setting.
# See docs/COMPLIANCE.md §2.
TWILIO_ACCOUNT_SID=
TWILIO_AUTH_TOKEN=
TWILIO_PHONE_NUMBER=
LIVEKIT_URL=
LIVEKIT_API_KEY=
LIVEKIT_API_SECRET=
OPENAI_API_KEY=

# Embeddings (task 6.6). `HashingEmbedder` is the only `Embedder` bound — a bag-of-words
# stand-in with **no semantics**: "how much do you charge" and "what does it cost" score
# zero against each other. So `SIMILARITY_FLOOR` (0.15) is calibrated against a fake, which
# is to say against nothing. Neither Anthropic nor Groq serves embeddings.
EMBEDDINGS_API_KEY=

# Auth (task 7.6). The seam is built (`TenantResolver`); isolation lives in the database, so
# binding Clerk changes one file and nothing below it.
CLERK_SECRET_KEY=
NEXT_PUBLIC_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=

# Billing. `packages/billing` computes an invoice and charges nobody.
STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=
